<title>NEW ZEALAND: Apple Fields half year loss expands.</title>
<headline>Apple Fields half year loss expands.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half yr result to Mar 31</p>
<p>			   (million NZ$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net loss				5.48 vs 2.00 loss</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)			  loss 18.7 vs 6.9 loss</p>
<p>    Turnover				    2.34 vs 6.93</p>
<p>    Pretax loss				 5.48 vs 3.08 loss</p>
<p>    Equity earnings			    0.0 vs 1.08</p>
<p>    Shares outstanding (million)	 29.25 vs same</p>
<p>Note - Apple Fields Ltd is currently in the process of becoming a specialist property developer after exiting its apple orcharding business.</p>
<p>The company said its half year report reflected this transition, and included one-off costs associated with the move.</p>
<p>Apple Fields said the changes should move it into a position of positive operating cashflows over the next year, with break even to increasing profits expected as its village development programme progressed.</p>
<p>The company intends to reduce debt to between $15-$20 million through the sale of non core asset such as its shareholding in Dairy Brands and the progressive sale of rural residential lots available on the outlying orchards. --Wellington Newsroom (64 4) 4734746</p>
</text>
